/*
 * clip-backend-config.h.example - Template for the private backend
 * credentials Clip Creation needs
 *
 * Copy this file to clip-backend-config.h (which is gitignored) and fill
 * in your own values. Clip Creation needs a backend that:
 *   1. Stores each user's Rumble API URL, queryable via a REST API scoped
 *      to that user (the default implementation uses a Supabase table
 *      named rumble_credentials with a user_id column and RLS policies
 *      keyed on a caller-supplied bearer token — see
 *      ClipManager::fetchRumbleApiUrl() in clip-manager.cpp).
 *   2. Accepts POST requests to create a clip, given a video ID, a
 *      duration in seconds, and a user ID (see
 *      ClipManager::createClip() in clip-manager.cpp for the exact
 *      request/response shape expected).
 *
 * Without a real, compatible backend behind these values, Clip Creation
 * compiles and loads fine but every clip attempt will simply fail (network
 * errors logged to the OBS log) — same as helixtools-restream before it
 * had a destinations editor.
